From 8052b01a00bec9d511e1c60b4b994024db183376 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:40:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Keep held marks and recent mark ids on the character, so
 a restart loses neither

A held mark (soak, Circle of Protection, Death Defy) and the ids of the
marks a desk sent lived in the marks handler's memory, so a restart lost the
mark, and a stale card's decline then landed the mark it named by the
restart rule (#17, #18). They are now stored in characters.held_mark (the
held record with its offer and offer_id) and characters.taken_mark_ids
(the last 16), each committed with the mark. After a restart the desk that
opens gets the same offer with the same offer_id. An answer naming an offer
the server does not hold lands nothing and is answered with
mark_offer_closed {offer_id, dropped: true}, so the desk closes that card.
The ally offers kept in memory expire with their existing refusals.

The sheet now carries held_marks {ability, mark_types} (also on GET
/api/investigators/{id}), and each offer sends the Lightkeeper the sheet
(manager.show_gm_sheet), so her copy can draw the held marks (#23). A death
drops the held mark in the scar's own commit.

Checked with test_ws_marks (the restart test flipped, a held mark and a
Death Defy count surviving a restart, ally offers expiring, mark ids after a
restart, the Lightkeeper's sheet), test_investigators, test_surface with the
openapi snapshot regenerated, test_ws_character, test_access,
test_ws_gm_view, test_rest_broadcasts, test_ws_rolls and test_ws_circle.

